import ../materials.dl
import reflections.dl
import shadows.dl

set point to the smooth shader interpolant named "world_position" at location 0 of type vector
set interpolated to the smooth shader interpolant named "world_normal" at location 1 of type vector
set local to the smooth shader interpolant named "local_position" at location 2 of type vector
set color to the smooth shader interpolant named "color" at location 3 of type @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set emission to the flat shader interpolant named "emission" at location 4 of type vector
set surface to the flat shader interpolant named "surface" at location 5 of type @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set flags to the flat shader interpolant named "flags" at location 6 of type (@intrinsic("vector", 4, @intrinsic("type", "uint", 32)))
set shadow to the smooth shader interpolant named "shadow_position" at location 7 of type @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set depth to the smooth shader interpolant named "view_depth" at location 8 of type a 32 bit floating-point number
set eye to the shader uniform named "eye_time" at binding 2 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set sun to the shader uniform named "sun" at binding 3 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set sunlight to the shader uniform named "sun_color" at binding 4 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set sky to the shader uniform named "hemisphere_sky" at binding 5 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set ground to the shader uniform named "hemisphere_ground" at binding 6 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set fog to the shader uniform named "fog" at binding 7 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set settings to the shader uniform named "shadow_settings" at binding 8 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set environment to the shader uniform named "environment" at binding 15 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set weather to the shader uniform named "weather" at binding 16 as @intrinsic("vector", 4)
set normal to interpolated normalized
if (the fragment is front facing) = false:
    set normal to normal * -1.0
# Derivatives execute for the entire fragment quad, before material branches.
set roughness to the UI scene standard roughness from (the element at 0 in surface) on normal normal
set base to a new vector with x (the element at 0 in color), y (the element at 1 in color) and z (the element at 2 in color)
if (the element at 0 in flags) = (1 as a 32 bit unsigned integer):
    set base to the website Farm cow coat on base at local
set radiance to base
if (the element at 1 in flags) = (0 as a 32 bit unsigned integer):
    set view to ((a new vector with x (the element at 0 in eye), y (the element at 1 in eye) and z (the element at 2 in eye)) - point) normalized
    set light to a new vector with x (the element at 0 in sun), y (the element at 1 in sun) and z (the element at 2 in sun)
    set nl to (the dot product of normal and light) clamped between 0.0 and 1.0
    set nv to (the dot product of normal and view) clamped between 0.0 and 1.0
    set metalness to the element at 1 in surface
    set first to the website Farm scattering at roughness roughness cosine nv
    set second to the website Farm scattering at roughness roughness cosine nl
    set fresnel to (the UI scene white radiance) * (0.04 * (1.0 - metalness)) + base * metalness
    set specular to the UI scene GGX reflection on normal viewed along view lit along light with Fresnel fresnel roughness roughness
    set dielectric to (the UI scene white radiance) * 0.04
    set compensation to (the UI scene direct scattering compensation from dielectric integrated for view first light second) * (1.0 - metalness)
    set compensation to compensation + (the UI scene direct scattering compensation from base integrated for view first light second) * metalness
    set reflectance to the UI scene diffuse reflectance of base at metalness metalness
    set visibility to 1.0
    if (the element at 3 in flags) != (0 as a 32 bit unsigned integer):
        set visibility to the website Farm shadow at shadow using settings
    set direct to (a new vector with x (the element at 0 in sunlight), y (the element at 1 in sunlight) and z (the element at 2 in sunlight)) * ((the element at 3 in sun) * (nl * visibility))
    set radiance to direct * ((reflectance + specular) + compensation * (the UI scene reciprocal pi))
    set upper to a new vector with x (the element at 0 in sky), y (the element at 1 in sky) and z (the element at 2 in sky)
    set lower to a new vector with x (the element at 0 in ground), y (the element at 1 in ground) and z (the element at 2 in ground)
    set hemisphere to the UI scene hemisphere light on normal from sky upper ground lower along (a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0)
    set radiance to radiance + hemisphere * reflectance
    if (the element at 0 in flags) = (2 as a 32 bit unsigned integer):
        set direction to normal * (2.0 * (the dot product of normal and view)) - view
        set direction to (direction * (1.0 - roughness * roughness) + normal * (roughness * roughness)) normalized
        set maximum to the element at 1 in environment
        set reflection to (the website Farm reflection along direction at level (roughness * maximum)) * (the element at 0 in environment)
        set irradiance to (the website Farm reflection along normal at level maximum) * (3.141592653589793 * (the element at 0 in environment))
        set radiance to radiance + (the UI scene environment diffuse on base at metalness metalness integrated as first lit by irradiance)
        set radiance to radiance + (the UI scene environment specular on base at metalness metalness integrated as first reflecting reflection lit by irradiance)
set radiance to radiance + emission
set {fog color} to a new vector with x (the element at 0 in fog), y (the element at 1 in fog) and z (the element at 2 in fog)
set radiance to the website Farm fogged color from radiance toward fog color at distance depth
set opacity to the element at 3 in color
if (the element at 0 in flags) = (3 as a 32 bit unsigned integer):
    set opacity to opacity * (the element at 0 in weather)
set the fragment color with a red channel of (the x of radiance), a green channel of (the y of radiance), a blue channel of (the z of radiance) and an alpha channel of opacity
